{
  "Name": "Linux Kernel recvmmsg Privilege Escalation",
  "Description": "This module attempts to exploit CVE-2014-0038, by sending a recvmmsg system call with a crafted timeout pointer parameter to gain root. This exploit has offsets for 3 Ubuntu 13 kernels: 3.8.0-19-generic (13.04 default); 3.11.0-12-generic (13.10 default); 3.11.0-15-generic (13.10). This exploit may take up to 13 minutes to run due to a decrementing (1/sec) pointer which starts at 0xff*3 (765 seconds)",
